{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1147560-time-magic-paradox-question","id":1147560,"title":"Time Magic/Paradox Question","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-10-06T13:21:52-07:00","id":1147560,"title":"Time Magic/Paradox Question","content":"In our on-going campaign a player sped time in their sanctum so that it passed within at an increased speed (60 times normal). The effect only lasts for 1 month (divided successes). Since this causes five years to pass within the span of one month my thoughts are that any person residing within when the effect ends would be subject to massive paradox. However I do not want to be too harsh and so thought I would ask the community. What are your opinions?<br /> <br /> Edit: Fixed wording to be consistent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13741-xarknor","user":"Xarknor","date":". 10-06-2017, 05:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13741-xarknor","name":"Xarknor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-06T13:47:41-07:00","id":1147572,"title":"","content":"Why would it have any effect at all? The effect was contained within the Sanctum. Or would you also apply paradox because someone burned something using magic in a Sanctum?<br /> <br /> The whole point of a Sanctum is that everything is Coincidental there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-06T14:19:30-07:00","id":1147579,"title":"","content":"Wait, did they slow down time or speed it up? You say slowed, but then use the phrase &quot;increased speed&quot;. Did you mean decreased?<br /> <br /> Assuming you mean decreased, I would not apply Paradox until 50 years have gone by without them aging. At that point I would give the character 1 point of permanent Paradox per 50 years of age they have avoided. The effect itself is coincidental within their Sanctum, but that only grants you so much wiggle room. Some effects, like severe body modification, give you permanent Paradox even if the casting itself is coincidental.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12710-pazuzuaxelf","name":"PazuzuAxelf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-06T14:59:07-07:00","id":1147590,"title":"","content":"Sorry yes they increased time in the Sanctum. And while in there they had a cadre of people crafting gadgets and trinkets, in addition to the normal learning.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13741-xarknor","name":"Xarknor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-06T16:27:31-07:00","id":1147609,"title":"","content":"I think that a person entering a building and exiting a month later 5 years older is within the realm of Coincidence, since that's a time frame that isn't as noticeable in people. Some people can end up looking years older or younger because of changes in their stress levels, lifestyle, health issues, or even how they apply make-up. Unless we're talking about child characters - for whom 5 years can mean the world of difference - a Hypothetical Average Observer might not notice how the character has aged, or might easily rationalize it if they did. It's been a month, after all. Anything can happen in a month. The only hitch I can think of is that if a character lets their hair grow out for all that time, it might raise questions. So the characters should make sure they've cut it to a length that's reasonable for one month's growth, or just make it shorter and imply a haircut.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-06T19:21:23-07:00","id":1147642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xarknor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1147560-time-magic-paradox-question?p=1147590#post1147590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry yes they increased time in the Sanctum. And while in there they had a cadre of people crafting gadgets and trinkets, in addition to the normal learning.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aaaand? They shortened their lives by FIVE YEARS.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-06T23:38:30-07:00","id":1147691,"title":"","content":"So then a mage could do this and learn/improve five years worth of attributes, spheres, talents, skills, knowledge, and arete in a month without consequence?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13741-xarknor","name":"Xarknor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-06T23:44:12-07:00","id":1147692,"title":"","content":"Well.<br /> <br /> For the mage, that are still five years passing. This is important to remember. From their point of view, they are spending *Five years!* in that sanctum.<br /> I'd go for some serious willpower rolls if they are even remotely social, to see if they last that long in there. And even if they manage to stay, five years of isolation changes people. Probably for the worse, too.<br /> <br /> <br /> I also hope they have enough food in that Sanctum, and as I said enjoy not having contact with the rest of humanity for that time from their point of view. I'm sure the boss will want to know where they went, too, for that whole month.<br /> <br /> Really, this only works for antisocial characters that have no ties to anyone or anything except maybe their cabalmates (if they are also present), don't want to interact with sleepers, have no obligations to their traditions they need to take care of, hold no strict job, have no mundane belongings that needs regular tending, and..well. Are pretty much utter hermits. Life of the party. Last but not least they need to be lucky for the Avatar not to scream utter rage into their ears.<br /> <br /> And speaking of Avatars, gaining Arete or Spheres is not a function of simply time passing. It takes enlightenment. Study. Mentoring. Revealed knowledge and trials.<br /> And all of that often enough hardly works in isolation, nor is pulling away from the world enlightening in most cases.<br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> To add, this is the kind of stuff Archmages pull off that have lost their ties to most of the world already, and are urgently trying to solve deeper mysteries without the world continuing to turn. There is also a reason Archmages are often considered too narrow-minded and focused on a thing they obsess about, to actually head for Ascension anytime soon.<br /> <br /> That said, slowing down time in a Sanctum *Can* be a great tool to solve a problem that has a very very narrow and hard time limit. It's a good idea for that.<br /> But spending five years in there is..not something I see most willworkers willing (heh) or able to do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 10-07-2017, 03:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-06T23:46:41-07:00","id":1147693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xarknor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1147560-time-magic-paradox-question?p=1147691#post1147691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So then a mage could do this and learn/improve five years worth of attributes, spheres, talents, skills, knowledge, and arete in a month without consequence?</div> </div> </div> </div>If they wanted to, sure. If they wanted to be cooped up in a single building for five years, more power to them. Not sure how well they'd handle the cabin fever, though. Or how they won't have access to things like social media or their loved ones, as they exist in a different timescale.<br /> <br /> Experience needed to actually raise Traits might be an issue, if the characters are compressing time so heavily. XP is usually awarded per session or storyline, not per month spent in study. What the characters are doing, here, is basically engaging in downtime...just, you know, sped up versus the rest of the world. And downtime, while good for <i>justifying</i> Trait increases, is not necessarily great for getting the XP needed to actually <i>buy</i> them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-09T12:38:49-07:00","id":1148398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Experience needed to actually raise Traits might be an issue, if the characters are compressing time so heavily. XP is usually awarded per session or storyline, not per month spent in study. What the characters are doing, here, is basically engaging in downtime...just, you know, sped up versus the rest of the world. And downtime, while good for </span><i>justifying</i><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> Trait increases, is not necessarily great for getting the XP needed to actually </span><i>buy</i><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> them.</span></div> </div> </div> </div> Indeed, if you have the PX, training in your &quot;time chamber&quot; may be the excuse you need to increase that Trait without using a lot of downtime.<br /> <br /> As has been said, logistics can be an issue: You need all the materials and people you're going to need, because each time you leave your &quot;time room&quot; you switch to normal time and that's, perhaps, months of whatever you were doing you've just wasted to buy groceries or whatever (don't expect to be able to send someone to buy the stuff if you can't wait months for their return!)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">And speaking of Avatars, gaining Arete or Spheres is not a function of simply time passing. It takes enlightenment. Study. Mentoring. Revealed knowledge and trials.<br /> And all of that often enough hardly works in isolation, nor is pulling away from the world enlightening in most cases.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree, many if not most mystical practices heavily recomend isolation. From the priests that would isolate into a remote monastery, to japanese yamabushi buddhists, the practice of cutting your ties with the rest of the world it's honed in many traditions that revere the mystical stuff that it's often called &quot;enlightenment&quot;. There's a lot of ascetic practices that involve living in isolation for a time (to gain &quot;enlightenment&quot;), but the histories of the wise hermit are so extensive as to get it's own Tarot card...Mage favors to tell stories within a social context, where the characters interact with the humane world and do stuff because being a hermit isn't very <i>entertaining </i>(which it's very different), but stating that &quot;pulling away from the world&quot; isn't enlightening makes me wonder from which Paradigm do you come to say such a thing. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-09T14:50:56-07:00","id":1148446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1147560-time-magic-paradox-question?p=1148398#post1148398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I disagree, many if not most mystical practices heavily recomend isolation. From the priests that would isolate into a remote monastery, to japanese yamabushi buddhists, the practice of cutting your ties with the rest of the world it's honed in many traditions that revere the mystical stuff that it's often called &quot;enlightenment&quot;. There's a lot of ascetic practices that involve living in isolation for a time (to gain &quot;enlightenment&quot;), but the histories of the wise hermit are so extensive as to get it's own Tarot card</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yes. Quite, there *are* those practices, but you already need to have a certain level of enlightenment to make use of that state - one could even say that being able to cut all those ties in the first place is a further step towards enlightenment, not the beginning. And usually the cliche hermit you find is old, and probably for good reason <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> As I said, it is a very ArchMage thing to do, too - there are lots of references in Masters of the Art that it is a common thing of Archmages to leave society and the world behind them. But you can't toss a young mage into a hermit lifestyle and expect them to become wise anytime soon. The young ones need a teacher - and that in turn isn't being at true hermit.<br /> <br /> Asceticism is not quite the same coin - asceticism can work early, and does not necessarily require you to isolate yourself from the society at large. See the cliche of the 'poor' monk traveling the land and helping people, but not having any wordly possessions to speak of. The Akashics are big on it - some Verbena probably, too, as are certain kinds of Choristers, no doubt. Asceticism is much more widespread than being a hermit.<br /> <br /> <br /> Oh, and as for your last question -. the same reason I doubt that being a hermit leads you to Ascension in mage is the very fact that ArchMages do it a lot - the same kind of Mages that, as stated multiple times, are in very high danger and have a high tendency to leave the path to Ascension without noticing, in their obsessive quest for knowledge and power. I doubt that is a coincidence right there.<br /> Now, being a hermit can lead you to knowledge - to power over the spheres, to enlightenment in the form of Arete under your isolated studies.<br /> But Ascension? There are strong indications that being a hermit might not the quite way to that.<br /> I also don't think that, unless you are a Mage with a certain established base of knowledge - an Adept at least - that you will be able to study well on your own in isolation. Adepts (maybe), Masters and Archmages are enlightened enough to march forward on their own. But younger mages probably are not - else being an Orphan would not, at all, be a hindrance to learning.<br /> <br /> ..granted, in M20 it isn't, anymore. So there's that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 10-09-2017, 05:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-11T07:21:56-07:00","id":1148811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh yes. Quite, there *are* those practices, but you already need to have a certain level of enlightenment to make use of that state. - one could even say that being able to cut all those ties in the first place is a further step towards enlightenment, not the beginning. And usually the cliche hermit you find is old, and probably for good reason</div> </div> </div> </div>No, you don't need to be old, much less enlightened, to be in a secluded monastery. I don't know why you would think that. As I said, budhist practicioners do this kind of thing, relatively young buddhists are able to do this temporarily (like, for a week), and they would answer something akin to &quot;no&quot; if you asked if they're enlightened (like, &quot;maybe everyone it's enlightened it's just they don't realize&quot;, which to me means no, but whatever). Why these youngsters decide to go somewhere secluded to\u00b7live without the distractions of normal society for a short time? well, it's part of their practice.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As I said, it is a very ArchMage thing to do, too - there are lots of references in Masters of the Art that it is a common thing of Archmages to leave society and the world behind them. </div> </div> </div>Which never implies that isn't for other mages too. We have a &quot;hermit&quot; just near the &quot;rogue&quot; and &quot;orphan&quot; in the Basic when it talks about unaligned mages. It never says that you need to be beyond Adept to even try.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But you can't toss a young mage into a hermit lifestyle and expect them to become wise anytime soon. The young ones need a teacher - and that in turn isn't being at true hermit.<br /> </div> </div> </div>And can you tell me why you think this issolation has to be done without your teacher?. The OP never specified that the &quot;time chamber&quot; it's small or that it only has space for one person. If fact, it's supposed to have a workshop inside. Nothing impedes a powerful Master from building a Realm outside of time where young Akashicks can go and live their Paradigm outside normal society.<br /> <br /> Also, you're wrong. It's wrong to think all starting player characters of Mage need a teacher to increase Spheres/Arete. It helps, but you're supposed to have ended your basic training, otherwise Mentor background would be mandatory for every Traditionalists as every Traditionalist has to be intorduced in the Tradition by a teacher.<br /> <br /> Any self respecting Hermetic Disciple should be able to do research and kick the library for himself in order to reach new heights of power, as can be seen in Ars Magica and shown by the fact that you've gained your Name and pass the exam that introduces you in the world of Mages. It helps to have a mentor, but I don't understand why people assumes that a starting character of mage it's a total newbie. There's a book (Aprentices of the Art) if you want to play a total newbie. Virtual Adepts value people that are self taught. It's wrong to say that until you're an old master you can't increase Arete/Spheres without the advantages mentorship. A Mentor helps, but so does a Library, or even a potent Avatar, among other things.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I also don't think that, unless you are a Mage with a certain established base of knowledge - an Adept at least - that you will be able to study well on your own in isolation. Adepts (maybe), Masters and Archmages are enlightened enough to march forward on their own. But younger mages probably are not - else being an Orphan would not, at all, be a hindrance to learning. </div> </div> </div>Why not?. You don't need to be enlightened at all, sleepers do this all the time and I would think it would be very thematic for many paradigms to awaken during such isolation, or to do a Search (the monk that to increase enlightement (Arete) goes to a monastery to meditate for a week expecting a revelation).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Asceticism is not quite the same coin - asceticism can work early, and does not necessarily require you to isolate yourself from the society at large </div> </div> </div>But it <i>often does</i>, as with Chorister who are big on the secluded monastery thing, or Verbena that live in the woods (don't the have a whole camp more or less based arround this?).<br /> <br /> And even when it doesn't, ascets may do it for a time to get better at asceticism. I would think that it would be very thematic for Akashic training at some point of the apprenticeship (the clasic trope of the master leaving the student in the mountain and saying &quot;survive there alone for a month&quot;, as to put the apprentice in a very extreme situation in order for her to unlock her hidden potential. A perfectly good moment to Awaken).<br /> <br /> If you can or can't reach Ascencion (that's kinda vague and may or may not depend on Paradigm) this way it's irrelevant, as we were talking about increasing Arete/Spheres within a chamber that isolates you from the outer world (but not necessarily alone, I would think!, I even mentioned people in my post), which I think any mage with the right Paradigm should be able to do without a mentor regardless of current Arete (albeit having a Mentor does help).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 10-11-2017, 10:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-11T16:16:05-07:00","id":1148923,"title":"","content":"I actually built one of those rooms on a smaller scale during a Mage game. The room was 7x faster, a day equalled a week inside, and the way my storyteller ran it, it was trippy as all else. My mages sleeping pattern went haywire, was tired almost all the time, would use up the group's food stores really quickly making him fairly unpopular, and would eventually loose all frames of reference to time. Aging wasn't as pressing an issue, but it was constantly brought up as a hazard to extended use.<br /> He'd often emerge only to find it was the middle of the night, and no one was about.<br /> <br /> Also, they started to introduce strange creatures just out of the corners of the room, watching me curiously the longer I stayed in the room, almost as though there was something living in the corners of the time stream, and my room had caught their attention.<br /> But the question of whether they were real or just the product of a mind isolated from normal time was never concluded.<br /> <br /> None of this was paradox, just concequence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":12193,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","user":"Saikou","date":". 10-11-2017, 07:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-11T21:19:08-07:00","id":1148989,"title":"","content":"I agree with Aleph. Characters - not just Masters, but any character - gaining greater understanding by retreating from the world is a venerable meme, in many different magical styles. Even Etherites can do it, locking themselves in their lab for days or weeks, with nothing but a chalk board, a desk stacked with papers and research texts, and plentiful experimental equipment. All before they shout &quot;EUREKA! I'VE GOT IT!&quot;, and emerge, emaciated and sleep deprived, but with a wild look in their eyes. Like they've just grasped hold of that most elusive of traits: Genius!<br /> <br /> Not only would a madboy not need a Master giving them advice, the Etherite might consider them an <i>impediment</i> to their research. Every member of the Society of Ether makes of Science(!) what they will, independently. That is the nature of Progressive Science. Having an older member around would just get in the way, and the venerable Master scientist has their own research. If the youngster still wants or needs assistance, he can ask for it, but a fully inducted member of the Tradition should be trusted to make their own way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-12T06:45:18-07:00","id":1149076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1147560-time-magic-paradox-question?p=1148923#post1148923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, they started to introduce strange creatures just out of the corners of the room, watching me curiously the longer I stayed in the room, almost as though there was something living in the corners of the time stream, and my room had caught their attention.<br /> But the question of whether they were real or just the product of a mind isolated from normal time was never concluded.<br /> <br /> None of this was paradox, just concequence.</div> </div> </div> </div>I always liked the idea that there were *entities* in the time stream that can interfere with time travelers. This was implied in Time 5 writeup, but never explored. I think that a lasting time distortion attracting the atention of said beings would be interesting.<br /> <br /> Someone may actually try to repeat the experiment in order to meet these things, after all, mystics often do isolation to start &quot;hallucinating&quot; just like that. To meet with terrifying *things* it's the stuff of the shaman. Somebody's &quot;product of the mind&quot; may be the sacred spirits of someone else's, but how can one be sure that the experience was &quot;real&quot;? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 10-12-2017, 09:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-12T07:38:28-07:00","id":1149095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1147560-time-magic-paradox-question?p=1149076#post1149076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I always liked the idea that there were *entities* in the time stream that can interfere with time travelers. This was implied in Time 5 writeup, but never explored. I think that a lasting time distortion attracting the atention of said beings would be interesting.<br /> <br /> Someone may actually try to repeat the experiment in order to meet these things, after all, mystics often do isolation to start &quot;hallucinating&quot; just like that. To meet with terrifying *things* it's the stuff of the shaman. Somebody's &quot;product of the mind&quot; may be the sacred spirits of someone else's, but how can one be sure that the experience was &quot;real&quot;? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Sapphire and Steel have been assigned...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-12T08:49:08-07:00","id":1149129,"title":"","content":"Wrinkle was a Paradox spirit for time and he will beat up those who abuse Time magick. . ..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-12T10:23:55-07:00","id":1149155,"title":"","content":"But Paradox spirits won't bother you as long as you abuse inside your Sanctum and your abuse isn't against the Constants/Foundations. Wrinkle only cares if you abuse Time in a way that breaks Reality, which this particular working shouldn't be doing.<br /> <br /> The thing that I find interesting about &quot;time entities&quot;, it's that these entities of the time stream could go outside that logic, picking an interest on your doings in spite of you not breaking any of Reality's rules that mages know so well. They allow to throw an unexpected consequence that has nothing to do with Paradox and that may escalate outside Paradox logic (for instance, caring about what happens in your Sanctum, or presenting a problem even if you used Prime 5 to fend agains ol'dox).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-12T13:56:49-07:00","id":1149232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>baakyocalder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1147560-time-magic-paradox-question?p=1149129#post1149129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wrinkle was a Paradox spirit for time and he will beat up those who abuse Time magick. . ..</div> </div> </div> </div>Not necessarily. Wrinkle is quite an amicable and reasonable Paradox Spirit, all told. He politely asks the mage to stop doing what they're doing, and will offer to help them undo what they did to the time stream.<br /> <br /> It's only when you <i>refuse</i> his reasonable request that he starts having to play hard ball.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-13T00:18:11-07:00","id":1149335,"title":"","content":"I always suspected those Time creatures might be related in part to the Hounds of Tindalos.<br /> Needless to. Say, I did not want to stay in that room for too long after that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}